            <ArticleTitle>A skull base epidermoid cyst causing the symptoms of a craniomandibular disorder.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>203-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article describes a case report of a 52 year old patient with a ten year history of orofacial pain who was misdiagnosed with a craniomandibular disorder (CMD) and trigeminal neuralgia. After a epidermoid cyst in the skull base had been diagnosed and removed the complaints diminished and finally disappeared.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
